plaso.tsv.gz: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from tests/fixtures/plaso/Catalog1.edb with its esedb/file_history plugin, one
line per event, sorted: identifier, parent identifier, original filename, file
attributes, USN, the time as a FILETIME (empty for "Not a time") and the
time's description. Written from plaso's output, not from this crate.

On a Linux host with Docker, Catalog1.edb (uncompressed) in /tmp/smo/fh/in/:

    sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/smo/fh:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 log2timeline --status_view none -q --parsers 'esedb/file_history' --storage-file /data/out.plaso /data/in
    sudo docker run --rm -v /tmp/smo/fh:/data log2timeline/plaso:20260720 psort --status_view none -q -o json_line -w /data/out.jsonl /data/out.plaso

then, here:

    python3 -I tests/oracle/plaso_tsv.py out.jsonl > tests/oracle/plaso.tsv
    gzip -9n tests/oracle/plaso.tsv
